    "faq": {
      "type": "sp-pdp-faq",
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "COMMON INQUIRIES",
        "heading": "Questions About Manual Manipulators"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "faq_1": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I upgrade the probe arm on my manipulator later?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. The probe arm mounts to a dovetail faceplate, so it can be swapped without replacing the manipulator body. Check the compatibility table above first: each model supports a different set of arm types, and the high-frequency arms require a magnetic base on the MA-9000 and MA-9100.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the difference between 80 TPI and 100 TPI lead screws?",
            "answer": "<p>Threads per inch sets how far the stage moves per turn of the drum, and so how finely you can place a probe. The 80 TPI MA-9000 resolves to 1 µm; the 100 TPI MA-9100 resolves to 0.35 µm. Choose 100 TPI for sub-micron structures and 80 TPI where 1 µm is sufficient.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are SemiProbe manipulators compatible with non-SemiProbe probe stations?",
            "answer": "<p>In most cases, yes. Magnetic bases hold on any ferromagnetic platen, vacuum bases need house vacuum at the station, and bolt-down bases need a matching hole pattern. Send us your platen details and we will confirm fit before you order.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What mounting base should I choose for high-frequency measurements?",
            "answer": "<p>Bolt-down, wherever the station allows it: a rigid mechanical mount gives the best stability for RF, microwave and millimetre-wave work, and the MA-8500 is built around it. Where bolt-down is not an option, a magnetic base is the next best choice; the West/East and North/South high-frequency arms are supported on magnetic bases on the MA-9000 and MA-9100.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_5": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do manipulators come calibrated?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Every unit ships with NIST-traceable calibrated vernier drums to NIST Standard Class A, and the lead time is 2 to 3 weeks after receipt of order.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "faq_1",
        "faq_2",
        "faq_3",
